ASSISTANT The string starts right after `''` — the first line is empty (newline right after `''`), then "  line1\n  line2\n  " and closing. Nix's rule: it strips the minimal indentation across all lines that contain non-whitespace, excluding the first line (the fragment right after `''`) and the last (the fragment right before closing `''`). So with all content lines at 2 spaces, it strips 2 spaces. Result: "line1\nline2\n". 
